    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n104200" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοιχώρῠχ-ος</span></b>  (parox.), ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖχος, ὀρύσσω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one who digs through the
			wall,</i> i.e. <i>housebreaker, burglar,</i> sts. as term of
			abuse, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				1327
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ra.</u>
				773
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Pl.</u>
				204
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Amips.
				24
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. καὶ ἱερόσυλοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					831e
				</span></i>
			: as Adj., of things, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὦ τοιχωρύχον λαγύνιον</span>”
				<i>rascally,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Diph.
					3.1
				</span></i>
			.</div>
